{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And there was a famine in the land, and Abram went down.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: the fathers are signs for the children. And this entire passage, in the events that befell our father Abraham, peace be upon him, is all a sign for his seed in the exile of Egypt: for the Egyptians took his wife, and the Holy One, blessed be He, took vengeance upon them with great plagues, and they brought him out of there with cattle, silver, and gold, and moreover Pharaoh commanded men concerning him to escort him away. And all of this befell the children. This is what our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded in Bereshit Rabbah: all that you find in Abraham you find in Israel. Concerning Abraham it is written ״ויהי רעב בארץ״ — and there was a famine in the land; and concerning Israel it is written (Genesis 45:6) ״כי זה שנתים הרעב״ — for these two years has the famine endured. Concerning Abraham it is written ״ותקח האשה בית פרעה״ — and the woman was taken into Pharaoh's house; and concerning Israel — they took their daughters, as it is said ״וכל הבת תחיון״ — and every daughter you shall keep alive. Concerning Abraham it is written (Genesis 12) ״וינגע ה׳ את פרעה״ — and HaShem plagued Pharaoh; and concerning Israel it is written (Exodus 11:1) ״עוד נגע אחד אביא על פרעה״ — yet one plague more I will bring upon Pharaoh. Concerning Abraham it is written (Genesis 12) ״ויקרא פרעה לאברם וגו׳ הנה אשתך קח ולך״ — and Pharaoh called Abram… behold your wife, take her and go; and concerning Israel it is written (Exodus 12:31) ״ויקרא למשה ולאהרן לילה ויאמר קומו צאו מתוך עמי״ — and he called for Moses and Aaron by night and said, rise up, get out from among my people. Concerning Abraham it is written (Genesis 12) ״ויצו עליו פרעה אנשים וישלחו אותו״ — and Pharaoh commanded men concerning him and they sent him away; and concerning Israel it is written (Exodus 12:33) ״למהר לשלחם מן הארץ״ — to hasten to send them out of the land. Concerning Abraham it is written (Genesis 13:2) ״ואברם כבד מאד במקנה בכסף ובזהב״ — and Abram was very heavy in cattle, in silver, and in gold; and concerning Israel it is written (Exodus 12:35) ״וישאלו ממצרים כלי כסף וכלי זהב״ — and they asked of the Egyptians vessels of silver and vessels of gold. Concerning Abraham it is written (Genesis 13:3) ״וילך למסעיו״ — and he went on his journeys; and concerning Israel it is written (Exodus 12:37) ״ויסעו בני ישראל מרעמס סכותה״ — and the children of Israel journeyed from Rameses to Succoth."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:08.982679819Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}